      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Clopidogrel is a new thienopyridine derivative and has less serious hematologic complications. We investigated the efficacy of clopidogrel plus aspirin (CA) in stent thrombosis prevention compared with ticlopidine plus aspirin (TA)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "METHOD AND RESULTS",
          "content": "Sixty-eight patients who underwent coronary stenting were randomized into 2 groups: TA group, n = 31 and CA group, n = 37. At 1 month, there were 3 major bleeding complications, 2 in the CA group and 1 in the TA group. Neither stent thrombosis nor hematologic events were found in both groups. Two patients in the TA group died, 1 from sudden death and another from tracheal stenosis. At 6 months, five patients developed in-stent restenosis, 4 in the CA group and 1 in the TA group, p = NS. One patient in each group had acute coronary syndrome."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Clopidogrel plus aspirin is an effective coronary stenting regimen comparable to ticlopidine plus aspirin."
        }
      ]},
